What this covers
----------------
Everything in this repository except:

  core/         mosh, as its authors published it: see LICENSE-MOSH.
  vendor/se1/   the SE1 guide, under its own terms (vendor/se1).
  vendor/tweetnacl/tweetnacl.c, tweetnacl.h
                TweetNaCl, in the public domain by its authors' statement
                (vendor/tweetnacl/README.md). The Makefile.am and the test beside
                them are gosh's.

Each file of gosh's carries one line that points here in place of a longer
notice.

Where gosh's files came from
----------------------------
gosh is the fork wmacevoy/mosh (at its tag mosh-1.4.0-pf.7) migrated into
named, tested parts. Many of its files were first written for that fork, in
2026, by the same copyright holder. In the fork they began with the notice mosh
puts on its own files ("Copyright 2012 Keith Winstein"), because they were
added to mosh's tree; none of them exists in mosh as its authors published it
(checked against mosh at commit decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da, which
is what core/ is). The owner of gosh, 2026-11-14: "only core is old code".

Two things in gosh do rest on mosh's own text, and LICENSE-MOSH applies to
that text:

  seam/*.patch          changes to mosh's files; the lines they keep and
                        replace are mosh's.
  src/command/moshwrapper.*
                        does what mosh's scripts/mosh.pl does, and uses some of
                        its words.

gosh is built on mosh and links with it; the combination is distributed under
